Position: .Net Full-Stack Developer (m/f/d)
Location: Available to candidates located in Poland
About Aras:
Backed by top-tier investors, Aras is one of the fastest growing privately-held Product Lifecycle Management (PLM) companies. We reinvent, engineer, and manufacture software to empower our customers with the flexibility to overcome tomorrow's challenges today. We have experienced steady growth year after year and are looking to accelerate Aras to the next level. We seek for the best people committed to making this a true success story and share in that glory. With our technology, our community, and the way we do business, we are transforming the way the world makes products. Our open, low-code technology enables greater scalability, flexibility, and security for the world's largest enterprises. Airbus, General Electric (GE), Hitachi, Honda, Kawasaki, and Microsoft are just a few of the organization's using our software. Aras targets a variety of industries including automotive, aerospace and defense, high-tech electronics, medical devices, and industrial manufacturing.
Who we are and what we do:
Aras Innovator is a dynamic product that has a flexible system of customization in accordance with specific needs and specific requirements, and this versatility is one of the reasons why our software is so successful around the world. Today, Aras suite is used by companies such as Microsoft, Airbus, Boeing, General Motors, Kawasaki, Motorola, Honda, Freudenberg, Imperial Tobacco Group, Schaeffler, ECCO, Carestream Health, GETRAG and other Fortune members.
We are looking for an experienced .Net Fullstack Developer to join our team that works on Aras Innovator - an industrial low-code platform for creating rich enterprise applications.
Requirements:

• Higher technical education;

• 10+ years of experience in commercial projects;

• C # knowledge, experience in .NET;

• OOP, SOLID principles understanding;

• Experience with MS SQL Server and good command of T-SQL;

• Experience with React;

• Good knowledge of web technologies (HTML, JavaScript/TypeScript);

• Knowledge of design patterns;

• Strong knowledge of Agile;

• Understanding of the HTTP protocol, REST, and OData;

• Possession of Git (or other DVCS);

• Upper-intermediate (reading/writing/speaking) levels;

• Strong team player with excellent collaboration and communication skills, committed to continuous improvement of team processes

• Ability to quickly switch between different contexts.

Desirable:

• Knowledge of TDD, experience in creating Integration tests;

• Experience in business correspondence;

• MongoDB

• Knowledge of Azure or AWS.

Must be eligible to work in Poland

